{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-506", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/506", "wordCount": 1601, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Hello everyone. My name is Shiva Sundar, and I'm"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "extremely excited to talk about"}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "HEVC Video with Alpha."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "You're probably familiar with"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "Alpha channels in image files today."}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "Alpha channels are ubiquitous"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "in image files, in our apps and on"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "the web."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "When there's an Alpha channel"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "in an image file, every pixel in the"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "image gets opacity along with"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "its color."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "This allows us to have an image"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "that has a complex,"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "non-rectangular shape but looks"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "natural when composited against"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "many different backgrounds."}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "So Alpha and transparency are"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "common and used all over the web"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "principally by still image"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "formats like PNG."}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "Alpha in video has been less"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "common."}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "It has been a professional video"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "workflow tool."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "The formats used in professional"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "video workflows like Apple"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "ProRes 4444 are very high data"}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "rate and not appropriate for"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "delivery."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "In 2017, Apple introduced"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "support for the HEIF image file"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "format, which lets us take"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "advantage of the advanced"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "lossy compression"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "technologies in HEVC to compress"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "still images."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "HEIF also lets you include an"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "Alpha channel in image files."}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "In fact, this year we are"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "adding support for HEIF"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "sequences, which lets you have"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "multiple images in a single"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "HEIF sequences also support"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "Alpha channels."}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "For some time we've recognized"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "the need for a lower bitrate way"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "to include Alpha in motion"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "video."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "And so we said let's use that"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "advanced loosy compression"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "technology to support Alpha"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "channels in video files as well."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "Playback of HEVC video with"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "Alpha is supported in iOS 13,"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "tvOS 13 and macOS Catalina on"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "all supported devices and"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "computers."}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "Encoding is supported on all of"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "those devices and computers that"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "have an HEVC encoder."}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "Having a video with Alpha format"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "that works well at bit rates low"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "enough for distribution opens up"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "many opportunities."}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "You can have rich,"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "non-rectangular motion video"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "content that you incorporate as"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "a layer as part of your app's"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "expressive experience."}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "It could be pre-rendered like an"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "animation."}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "Such an element can move around"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "on top of a complicated"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "background and you could even have"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "several of them to give a"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "feeling of depth or complex"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "interactions."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "Because these are movies they"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "can have synchronized sound"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "tracks so the characters in"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "these non-rectangular movies can"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "talk."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "Highly professional."}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "Alpha channel."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "Content."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "For you."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "Woo-hoo."}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "Woo-hoo."}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "They could be integrated into"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "games using SpriteKit, SceneKit"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "or Metal."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "In this context, we have"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "provided you with some sample"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "code on how to record a SceneKit"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "scene into a HEVC video with"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "Alpha and how to render another"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "in a SpriteKit scene."}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "On web pages, they could bring"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "interactive elements to life."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "HEVC video with Alpha is"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "supported by Safari in iOS 13"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "and macOS Catalina."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "Safari can also tell the web"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "page whether this feature is"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "supported."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "For more information on using"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "the media capabilities API, be"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "sure to check out the What's New"}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "in Authentication, Safari and"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "WebKit video."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "The ability to distribute video"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "with Alpha at low bitrates opens"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "opportunities for authoring apps"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "to provide background removal."}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "Here I am in front of a green"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "sheet hung from the wall"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "recorded using an iPhone."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "I wish I was here."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "I used a custom video compositor"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "with a co-image filter to"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "replace the green pixels with"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "transparency and exported it to"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "a video with Alpha."}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "I wish I was here."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "And now I can overlay this video"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "on any background I like."}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "I wish I was here."}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "We are providing sample code"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "showing how to do this and write"}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "the resulting HEVC video with"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "Alpha movie."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "So how does this work?"}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "As you know, movie files contain"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "tracks of various media types."}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "A video track contains video"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "frames."}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "HEVC video with Alpha is"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "contained inside a single video"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "track in the movie."}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "In the single track, each frame"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "contains 2 parts called layers"}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "and each layer is compressed"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "using the HEVC codec."}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "The base layer contains the"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "colored image of the frame as"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "usual."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "The Alpha layer contains just"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "the Alpha channel of the frame."}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "This is done using special HEVC"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "syntax which identifies the 2"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "layers."}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "The HEVC rules for this syntax"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "mean that the HEVC decoder that"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "does not know how to handle the"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "Alpha layer will ignore it and"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "display the base layer alone."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "Let's move along and talk about"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "how to use it."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "HEVC with Alpha encoding is"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "integrated into numerous AV"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "Foundation APIs."}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "Let's look at content creation,"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "for example."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "You can render video frames with"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "Alpha in your application and"}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "use AVAssetWriter to encode them"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "and write them to a movie file."}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "You can use new presets"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "available with"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "AVAssetExportSession to"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "transcode video formats"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "containing Alpha including Apple"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "ProRes 4444 into HEVC with"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "Alpha."}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "These new HEVC presets have the"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "suffix with Alpha."}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "You can also use"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "AVAssettExportSession to burn"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "in a specific background color"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "converting a movie with Alpha"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "into a movie without Alpha, that"}, {"start": 458.0, "text": "will play on players that don't"}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "support HEVC with Alpha."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "Or you can also use the HEVC"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "with Alpha video encoder"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "directly via"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "VTCompressionSession."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "Looking at AVFoundation's"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "playback APIs, HEVC with Alpha"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "is supported by AVPlayer and"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "AVPlayerLayer for display in"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "your apps view hierarchy via"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "Core Animation, AppKit and UIKit."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "The video in AVPlayerLayer will"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "be displayed with a transparent"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "background and composed with the"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "rest of the layers and views."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "Alternatively you can access a"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "sequence of decoded video frames"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "directly using"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "AVPlayerItemVideoOutput."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "This is a great choice when you"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "want to incorporate those video"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "frames into a custom rendering"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "you're doing using Metal,"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "SpriteKit and other GPU-based"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "rendering APIs."}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "If you need to decode frames for"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "another purpose, you can use"}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "AVAssetImageGenerator directory"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "and individual frame of the"}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "movie as a CGImage with Alpha."}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "You can use AVAssetReader to"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "extract video frames for use in"}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "a non-playback workflow."}, {"start": 553.0, "text": "You can also use the HEVC with"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "Alpha video decoder directly via"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "VTDecompressionSession."}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "In short because HEVC with Alpha"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "is integrated into AVFoundation"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "at the level of a video codec,"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "it fits in well into all these"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "familiar API workflows."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "Now let us see how we can"}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "accomplish this in code."}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "When encoding a movie, when"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "configuring your AVAssetWriter"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "input or VTCompressionSession,"}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "use the video codec type HEVC"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "with Alpha."}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "This is a special signal that"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "the Alpha channel should be"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "encoded."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "The encoded file will have the"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "standard HEVC codec type."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "It will be backwards compatible."}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "An HEVC player that does not"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "understand Alpha will display"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "only the base video layer."}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "It will ignore the Alpha"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "portion."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "If you work with Alpha channels,"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "you may know that there are 2"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "strategies for how to write"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "video data to a file,"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "premultiplied Alpha or straight"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "Alpha, also known as"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "unassociated Alpha or"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "non-premultiplied Alpha."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "The tradeoffs between these"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "choices are beyond the scope of"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "this talk."}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "If you're familiar with these,"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "what you need to know is that"}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "both are supported."}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "If you're not similar with"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "these, we recommend the default,"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "which is premultiplied Alpha."}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "It's the natural choice in most"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "GPU-based rendering parts and it"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "scales better."}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "Now looking at the code, you may"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "specify the Alpha mode by either"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "configuring the compression"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "session or as a buffer"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "attachment."}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "As a safety mechanism if the"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "setting and the buffer"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "attachment are both specified"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "and they do not match, the"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "encoding operation will fail."}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "Our APIs require the"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "Alpha channel to be encoded with"}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "fixed quality because video"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "encoding artifacts in the Alpha"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "channel can be bothersome in"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "ways that the same artifacts"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "wouldn't be in the base layer."}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "Our APIs let you"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "control the base layers bitrate"}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "and the Alpha channel's quality"}, {"start": 706.0, "text": "separately if you need to."}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "Now, looking at the code you can"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "specify the Alpha layer quality"}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "using target quality for Alpha"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "parameter."}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "It is arranged between 0 and 1"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "where 1 means it is close to"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "lossless."}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "The bitrate parameter you"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "specify only applies to the base"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "layer and is ignored by the"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "Alpha layer."}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "To detect the presence of an"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "Alpha channel, you can either"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "test AV media characteristic"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "containsAlphaChannel or you"}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "can query the format description"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "extension contains Alpha"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "channel."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "If you are trying to export HEVC"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "with Alpha movie, use to"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "determine compatibility API to"}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "validate that Alpha is present"}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "in the source asset."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "This validation only takes the"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "source movie into account not"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "the video composition."}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "So you must skip it if you are"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "using a video composition to"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "generate a new Alpha channel"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "from sources that do not have"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "Alpha channels."}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "There are a lot of video players"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "in the ecosystem."}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "Many of them don't support HEVC"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "let alone HEVC with Alpha."}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "You can remove the Alpha channel"}, {"start": 792.0, "text": "by burning in a solid background"}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "color."}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "We have added some convenience"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "API and sample code to help"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "simplify this conversion."}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "If you're looking to build"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "support into a non-Apple media"}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "framework, we have published a"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "specification for an"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "interoperability profile that"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "you should read, but if you"}, {"start": 814.0, "text": "can't wait, here is a sneak"}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "peek."}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "To summarize, HEVC video with"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "Alpha is a cool new feature."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "It takes advantage of HEVC's"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "state of the art compression"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "technology."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "It is supported on iOS 13, tvOS"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "13 and macOS Catalina."}, {"start": 841.0, "text": "It takes advantage of hardware"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "acceleration on recent devices."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "It is well integrated into"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "AVFoundation for use in your apps."}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "It is also integrated in Safari"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "for use in your web experiences."}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "HEVC with Alpha brings us new"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "opportunities for creative"}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "expression for both developers"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "and users alike."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "We can't wait to see the ways"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "you can take advantage of it in"}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "your apps."}]}
